@bank all
// Head writer W (playtest 1, 0.63.2; seat X's walk-up conversations): what a crew member says when they walk up and
// stop beside you to start a conversation. Clearly to you, by how well they know you. Card lines (90 at most).
// Seat X reads lineFor(who, 'approach', ctx), falling back to 'greet'.

== approach
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. You're the new one, aren't you? I thought I'd come and say hello properly.
- Sorry, I'm being nosy. You're new? Welcome aboard. I'm {first}.
- {hi}! I keep seeing you about and never stopping. So, stopping. Hello.
- Excuse me. You're the new hand? I've heard good things. Well, things.   #funny
- {hi}. I wanted to say welcome before somebody else beat me to it.
- You look like you're settling in. Are you? Honestly?
? tier=acquaintance
- {hi}, {nick}. Got a minute? I've been meaning to come and find you.
- Oh good, it's you. I wanted to ask how your week's going.
- {hi}! I saw you from over there and thought, I'll go and say hello.
- There you are. Settling in all right? You look like you know your way now.
- {hi}, {nick}. Mind if I stop a minute? My feet need a rest anyway.   #funny
? tier=colleague
- {hi}, {nick}. I was hoping I'd catch you. How's it going?
- Oh, {nick}! Just the person. Tell me something good about your day.
- {hi}. You've been busy. I've seen you all over the ship.
- There you are! I was going to come and find you anyway.
? tier=friend
- {nick}! I came over the second I saw you. How are you?   #warm
- There you are. I've been saving up things to tell you.
- {hi}, {nick}. Got a minute for me? Good. I've got news.
- Oh, perfect. I was just thinking I hadn't seen you today.   #warm
? tier=close
- {nick}. Come here. How are you, really?   #warm
- There you are. Everything's better with you about.   #warm
- {hi}, {nick}. I was looking for you. No reason. Just was.   #warm
? time:evening
- {hi}, {nick}. Long day? Come and tell me about it.
? time:morning
- Morning, {nick}. Have you eaten? You look like you haven't.   #funny
